20,"padding-inline-end":20},"blocks":{"text_8gqRtV":{"type":"text","name":"t:names.text","settings":{"text":"<ul><li>Every year since 2001 we have planted 500 poplar or willow poles to help stabilise our steeper country and provide shade & shelter for livestock.  <\/li><li>At least one shelter belt is planted every year using locally sourced native tree and plant species.  These shelter belts provide animal welfare benefits by reducing exposure to wind-run, shelter from rain & shade in the dry summer months.  They also enhance bio-diversity, especially by providing a food source. <\/li><\/ul>","width":"100%","max_width":"none","alignment":"left","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"1rem","line_height":"loose","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}}},"block_order":["text_8gqRtV"]}},"block_order":["group_iwL9hQ","group_kgBihK"]}},"block_order":["group_xVtn8b"],"disabled":true,"custom_css":[".custom-section-content {margin-bottom: 20px;}"],"name":"Planting ","settings":{"content_direction":"column","vertical_on_mobile":true,"horizontal_alignment":"flex-start","vertical_alignment":"center","align_baseline":false,"horizontal_alignment_flex_direction_column":"flex-start","vertical_alignment_flex_direction_column":"center","gap":40,"section_width":"page-width","section_height":"","section_height_custom":50,"color_scheme":"","background_media":"none","video_position":"cover","background_image_position":"cover","border":"solid","border_width":1,"border_opacity":30,"border_radius":10,"toggle_overlay":false,"overlay_color":"#00000026","overlay_style":"solid","gradient_direction":"to top","padding-block-start":50,"padding-block-end":50}},"image_with_text_boxed_e3zrGc":{"type":"image-with-text-boxed","name":"Regenerating native bush","settings":{"main_heading":"Regenerating native bush","heading_size":"h2","sub_heading":"","main_text":"<ul><li>Remnant native bush areas, normally steep gullies, have been fenced off to exclude stock thereby allowing regeneration of the native bush.  In-fill planting, using eco sourced native trees, eg, Ngaio, Karaka, Southern Rata & Totara, have accelerated the regeneration. <\/li><li>A Totara woodlot, comprising some 300 trees, has already been planted in a retired gully, and further woodlots are planned.  This is the definition of a long-term environmental project, given Totara trees take at least 300 years to approach maturity! <\/li><\/ul>","button_text":"","button_link":"","left_image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/palliser-ridge-scene.jpg","image_height_mode":"match","image_aspect_ratio":"square","image_object_fit":"cover","image_min_height":0,"image_max_height":1200,"column_position":"right","mobile_reverse_columns":false,"column_ratio":"equal","content_alignment":"left","vertical_alignment":"top","column_gap":40,"section_width":"page-width","heading_font":"heading","text_font":"body","heading_size_desktop":40,"subheading_size_desktop":18,"text_size_desktop":16,"heading_size_mobile":32,"subheading_size_mobile":16,"text_size_mobile":14,"column_background_color":"#ffffff","column_padding":50,"column_padding_mobile":20,"column_border_radius":8,"color_scheme":"scheme-1","image_border_radius":8,"enable_animation":true,"animation_delay":"0.2s","padding-block-start":25,"padding-block-end":25,"padding-block-start-mobile":25,"padding-block-end-mobile":25}},"image_with_text_boxed_x4aDCm":{"type":"image-with-text-boxed","name":"Biodiversity corridors","settings":{"main_heading":"Biodiversity corridors","heading_size":"h2","sub_heading":"","main_text":"<ul><li>Our work is forming part of a wider community project to link the Aorangi Forest Park with the Remutaka Forest Park via secure bio-diversity “corridors” of indigenous flora & fauna.   <\/li><li>These corridors are fenced to exclude grazing stock and predator control within the corridors will reduce damage to native flora and provide a safer habitat for native fauna, in all, a boost for bio-diversity. <\/li><\/ul>","button_text":"","button_link":"","left_image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Hero.jpg","image_height_mode":"match","image_aspect_ratio":"square","image_object_fit":"cover","image_min_height":0,"image_max_height":1200,"column_position":"left","mobile_reverse_columns":false,"column_ratio":"equal","content_alignment":"left","vertical_alignment":"top","column_gap":40,"section_width":"page-width","heading_font":"heading","text_font":"body","heading_size_desktop":40,"subheading_size_desktop":18,"text_size_desktop":16,"heading_size_mobile":32,"subheading_size_mobile":16,"text_size_mobile":14,"column_background_color":"#ffffff","column_padding":50,"column_padding_mobile":20,"column_border_radius":8,"color_scheme":"scheme-1","image_border_radius":8,"enable_animation":true,"animation_delay":"0.2s","padding-block-start":25,"padding-block-end":25,"padding-block-start-mobile":25,"padding-block-end-mobile":25}},"image_with_text_boxed_cCGkJt":{"type":"image-with-text-boxed","name":"Regenerating native bush","settings":{"main_heading":"Wetlands","heading_size":"h2","sub_heading":"","main_text":"<ul><li>We have restored or constructed at least one wetland a year and plan to continue this programme.  Sites in low-lying, boggy areas, particularly in steep gullies with minor water-courses, are selected for retirement. <\/li><li>We are committed supporters of the Wairio Wetlands restoration project on the eastern shores of Lake Wairarapa.<\/li><\/ul>","button_text":"","button_link":"","left_image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/Screen_Shot_2026-06-23_at_9.11.00_AM.png","image_height_mode":"match","image_aspect_ratio":"square","image_object_fit":"cover","image_min_height":0,"image_max_height":1200,"column_position":"right","mobile_reverse_columns":false,"column_ratio":"equal","content_ali